  doi:10.1186/gb-2013-14-10-r115, under CC BY 2.0. Rewritten in C++ with
  a Newton M-step, Armijo line search and fit-status reporting.

R/bmiq_calibration.R (thresholds, class modes and quantile transformation)
  Derived from Steve Horvath's BMIQcalibration, his adaptation of Andrew
  Teschendorff's BMIQ v1.2 (Teschendorff et al. 2013). Horvath's version is
  the NORMALIZATION.R additional file published with Horvath S (2013),
  Genome Biology 14:R115, doi:10.1186/gb-2013-14-10-r115, under CC BY 2.0.
  Teschendorff's BMIQ
  code is also distributed under GPL-3 in the Bioconductor packages ChAMP and
  wateRmelon, which GPL (>= 3) covers.

Reference copies
  The source consulted during development is kept in the development
  repository (the dev/ directory, not part of the built package):
  dev/preprocessCore for the quantile normalization, and
  dev/bmiq-calibration-legacy.R (Horvath's BMIQcalibration, blc2 and
  betaEst2) for the BMIQ calibration and the beta-mixture EM.

